    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help with pallet stability. we are doing high-density racking in a warehouse and i'm worried about the stacks tipping if they aren't layered right. what's the best way to handle the center of gravity and should we be interlocking the pallets?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To achieve stability, it's essential to consider the center of gravity when stacking high-density racking. Aim to keep the center of gravity low by staggering the placement of pallets and nesting boxes. This can be accomplished by placing the heaviest boxes at the base of the rack and using smaller or lighter pallets stacked on top. Interlocking pallets can indeed help improve stability, as it creates a \"stiff\" structure that resists tipping.",
      "source": "target",
